# MLX models for --backend mlx on an Apple M3 Pro with 36 GB unified memory (first tester box, 2026-11-04).
#
# Format (lib/model_config.py, same three fields as models/*.txt):
#   <name>  <served-model>  <params>  hf:<repo>
#   served-model  the local MLX directory the server was started with (matched against the end of the absolute path
#                 the server lists), or "-" when it was started with the hf: repo itself (then the cached copy is used
#                 at whatever revision the cache holds). The harness only checks that it appears in /v1/models; it never
#                 asks the server to load anything.
#   params        max_ctx=N (tasks needing more are SKIPPED_CTX), thinking (system prompt for reasoning models),
#                 revision=<sha> (the Hugging Face commit measured; recorded with the results)
#
# Start the server on the Mac with the prompt cache off, so no answer reuses an earlier task's prefix (the harness checks
# usage.cached_tokens and records hardware.order_independent from it):
#   hf download <repo> --revision <sha> --local-dir ~/mlx-models/<dir>      (<dir> as in field 2)
#   mlx_lm.server --model ~/mlx-models/<dir> --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8085 --prompt-cache-size 0
# and reach it from the harness machine through an SSH tunnel (ssh -N -L 8085:127.0.0.1:8085 mac), never an open port.
#
# Sizes are the weights alone; macOS lets the GPU wire about 27 GB of 36 by default, and the KV cache, macOS and (when
# the tests also run on the Mac) dotnet/node/pytest share the rest. Expand to the larger ones only after measuring.
#
# Revisions and sizes read from Hugging Face 2026-11-04.

# Smoke test: small, the architecture mlx-lm has supported longest (4.3 GB).
qwen2.5-coder:7b-mlx  mlx-models/qwen2.5-coder-7b  max_ctx=32768,revision=019cc73c45c7  hf:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct-4bit

# Same base as this repo's qwen3.8:27b (38/38 on llama-server, one RTX 4090), 16.1 GB. Comparable results; reasoning
# stays off unless the run passes --think, as on llama-server.
qwen3.8:27b-mlx  mlx-models/qwen3.8-27b  max_ctx=32768,thinking,revision=10c35caafbb8  hf:mlx-community/Qwen3.8-27B-4bit

# A3B MoE, fast on Apple Silicon, 20.4 GB: run only after the 27B shows the memory headroom.
qwen3.6:35b-a3b-mlx  mlx-models/qwen3.6-35b-a3b  max_ctx=32768,thinking,revision=38740b847e4c  hf:mlx-community/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-4bit

# Not listed: gemma-4-31B-it-qat-4bit is 28.8 GB of weights, more than the ~27 GB the GPU may wire on a 36 GB Mac.
